From: LukeValen <panvk-eden@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 109] panvk: preserve 64-bit provoking-vertex CS call address

The generated CS function buffer can live above 4 GiB on Kbase SAME_VA.
Storing its GPU address in uint32_t truncated the high bits before cs_call,
causing a CS translation fault when the function was invoked.

A captured Eden fault had sideband 0xffdb3400 while the live function BO
was mapped at 0x5fffdb3000; offset 0x400 reconstructs exactly to
0x5fffdb3400, proving the high address bits were lost in this assignment.

Target: Eden Android / Mali-G615 MC6 / Kbase CSF v11

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index d5318c8..f9dab03 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -2236,7 +2236,7 @@ get_fb_descs(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
          uint32_t fn_idx = calc_fn_set_fbds_provoking_vertex_idx(cmdbuf);
          uint32_t fn_stride =
             dev->draw_ctx->fn_set_fbds_provoking_vertex_stride;
-         uint32_t fn_addr =
+         uint64_t fn_addr =
             dev->draw_ctx->fns_bo->addr.dev + fn_idx * fn_stride;
          cs_move64_to(b, addr_reg, fn_addr);
          cs_move32_to(b, length_reg, fn_stride);
